es in Fortran 77</source><edition>2nd Ed</edition><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, USA</publisher-loc><year>1996</year><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><fpage>279</fpage><lpage>280</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ijms-10-00761"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bacon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickinson</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simulation of Particle Motion and Stability in Concentrated Dispersions</article-title><source>Faraday Discuss. Chem. Soc</source><year>1983</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>178</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ijms-10-00761"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Urbina-Villalba</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Garc&#x000ed;a-Sucre</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Toro-Mendoza</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of Polydispersity and Thermal Exchange on the Flocculation Rate of O/W Emulsions</article-title><source>Mol. Simul</source><year>2003</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>404</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijms-10-00761"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verwey</surname><given-names>EJW</given-names></name><name><surname>Overbeek</surname><given-names>JThG</given-names></name></person-group><source>Theory of the stability of lyophobic colloids</source><edition>2nd Ed</edition><publisher-name>Dover Publications Inc</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, USA</publisher-loc><year>1948</year><fpage>100</fpage><lpage>185</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ijms-10-00761"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Urbina-Villalba</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Garc&#x000ed;a-Sucre</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the Secondary Minimum on the Flocculation Rate of Nondeformable Droplets</article-title><source>Langmuir</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>6675</fpage><lpage>6687</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16008374</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22-ijms-10-00761"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chandrasekar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stochastic Problems in Physics and Astronomy</article-title><source>Rev. Mod. Phys</source><year>1943</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>89</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b23-ijms-10-00761"><label>23.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kramer</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Brownian Motion in a Field of Force and the Diffusion Model of Chemical Reactions</article-title><source>Physica</source><year>1940</year><volume>VII</volume><fpage>284</fpage><lpage>304</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b24-ijms-10-00761"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fuchs</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>&#x000dc;ber die Stabilit&#x000e4;t und Aufladung der Aerosole</article-title><source>Z. Physik</source><year>1936</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>736</fpage><lpage>743</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b25-ijms-10-00761"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGown</surname><given-names>DN.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Parfitt</surname><given-names>GD</giv